    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d521">

                <pb facs="0706" n="606" xml:id="pg606"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">211.65/110</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Long</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 594</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1934-06-22"
                            >June 22, 1934</date>.<lb/>[Received July 5.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform the Department
                    that during a conversation this morning with Mr. Suvich, Undersecretary for
                    Foreign Affairs, I asked how their study of the extradition treaty was
                    progressing. He said that they were making headway and he hoped to be able to
                    talk to me soon.<anchor n="20" xml:id="d521-f1"/></p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Breckinridge Long</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d521-f1" n="20" xml:id="d521-f1-content">
                <p>No report of any further reply from the Italian Government regarding these
                    negotiations has been found in the Department files.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
